WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.545 --> 00:00:04.827
Tomás Reyes: Hi David, good morning. Can you hear me?

2
00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:13.170
David Barron: Hi Tomás, yes, I can hear you. Good morning. Is it okay if I record this? I'm terrible at remembering logistics.

3
00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:21.255
Tomás Reyes: Of course. I'll give you permission. Kai from the AV team is here too, he'll handle the technical part.

4
00:00:22.432 --> 00:00:23.532
Kai (UIST AV): Hi David.

5
00:00:24.794 --> 00:00:26.469
David Barron: Hi Kai. Okay, recording.

6
00:00:26.956 --> 00:00:35.206
Tomás Reyes: Great. So, this is the AV check for the Learning and Tutoring session, Wednesday the seventh. You're the second talk of four.

7
00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:41.884
Tomás Reyes: Fifteen minutes for the talk, five for questions, and we're strict, because the session is only eighty minutes.

8
00:00:42.602 --> 00:00:47.040
David Barron: Okay. Second of four. So I'd start about twenty minutes in?

9
00:00:47.946 --> 00:00:55.233
Tomás Reyes: The session starts at ten-thirty local. If the first talk runs on time, your slot is ten-fifty to eleven-ten.

10
00:00:55.371 --> 00:01:02.294
Tomás Reyes: I'll introduce you, so please send me one sentence of bio and the right pronunciation of your name.

11
00:01:02.741 --> 00:01:07.238
David Barron: It's "Barron" like the baron, nothing fancy. I'll send a sentence today.

12
00:01:15.977 --> 00:01:25.059
Tomás Reyes: Perfect. Timing cards: I'll hold up five minutes, two minutes, and then stop. At stop I'll let you finish your sentence, not your section.

13
00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:28.913
David Barron: Ha, okay, fair. Finish the sentence.

14
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.725
Tomás Reyes: Kai, do you want to do the technical part?

15
00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:49.678
Kai (UIST AV): Sure. So, David, you can present from the room laptop or plug in your own. Room laptop is Windows with PowerPoint and a PDF viewer.

16
00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:57.282
Kai (UIST AV): If you use your own, we have HDMI and USB-C at the lectern. Can I ask what you're presenting from?

17
00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:08.057
David Barron: Keynote on a Mac, but I can export to PowerPoint or PDF. I'd rather use my own laptop because there's a short video in the talk.

18
00:02:08.839 --> 00:02:17.175
Kai (UIST AV): That's fine. Own laptop is okay. Can you share your screen now so I can check the aspect ratio and the video?

19
00:02:17.751 --> 00:02:20.981
David Barron: Yeah, one second. Sharing. Can you see it?

20
00:02:21.869 --> 00:02:28.045
Kai (UIST AV): Yep, I see the title slide. Sixteen by nine, good. Can you jump to the video?

21
00:02:29.625 --> 00:02:35.149
David Barron: Okay, it's slide six. It's a forty-second clip of the replay timeline. Playing it now.

22
00:02:36.132 --> 00:02:41.456
Kai (UIST AV): I can see it but I'm not hearing audio. Did you check "share sound"?

23
00:02:42.847 --> 00:02:47.663
David Barron: Oh, no. Sorry. Let me stop and reshare. Okay, now with sound.

24
00:02:53.269 --> 00:03:01.013
Kai (UIST AV): Yes, now I hear it. In the room, audio from your laptop goes through the house system if you're on HDMI.

25
00:03:01.362 --> 00:03:06.110
Kai (UIST AV): With USB-C it should too, but bring the HDMI adapter just in case.

26
00:03:07.602 --> 00:03:11.026
David Barron: Okay, I'll bring my USB-C to HDMI dongle.

27
00:03:12.259 --> 00:03:14.699
Kai (UIST AV): Good. Do you use presenter view?

28
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.389
David Barron: Yeah, I have speaker notes.

29
00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:24.933
Kai (UIST AV): Then please make sure your display is set to extended, not mirrored, when you plug in.

30
00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:30.397
Kai (UIST AV): We'll have two minutes at the break before the session to test it.

31
00:03:31.094 --> 00:03:33.350
David Barron: Okay, extended. And a clicker?

32
00:03:34.095 --> 00:03:41.193
Kai (UIST AV): There's a clicker at the lectern, it works with any laptop, it's just a USB receiver. Or bring yours.

33
00:03:42.613 --> 00:03:45.151
David Barron: I'll use yours. One less thing.

34
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:52.849
Kai (UIST AV): Mic: you'll have a lavalier. Please clip it on the jacket or collar, not near the laptop fan.

35
00:03:52.965 --> 00:04:00.665
Kai (UIST AV): And if you walk away from the lectern, the lav still works, but stay in the lit area for the stream.

36
00:04:02.009 --> 00:04:03.257
David Barron: Wait, it's streamed?

37
00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:11.597
Tomás Reyes: Yes, the sessions are streamed for remote registrants and recorded. That's the other thing I wanted to mention.

38
00:04:11.758 --> 00:04:21.251
Tomás Reyes: Please upload your pre-recorded backup video to the conference portal by Monday the fifth. If anything goes wrong in the room, we play the backup.

39
00:04:25.103 --> 00:04:28.517
David Barron: Okay. Backup video by the fifth. Same fifteen minutes?

40
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:36.359
Tomás Reyes: Same length, at most fifteen. It doesn't have to be fancy, a screen recording with your voice is fine.

41
00:04:37.154 --> 00:04:43.691
David Barron: Okay, I recorded one last week, I just need to trim it. It's about sixteen minutes right now.

42
00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.258
Tomás Reyes: Please trim it. We cut at fifteen.

43
00:04:53.556 --> 00:04:54.738
David Barron: Ha, got it.

44
00:04:55.529 --> 00:05:04.351
Tomás Reyes: Questions. We'll have a mic runner in the room, and I'll read one or two remote questions from the Q&A channel if there's time.

45
00:05:04.583 --> 00:05:09.556
Tomás Reyes: If nobody asks anything, I usually have a question ready, so don't worry.

46
00:05:11.075 --> 00:05:17.277
David Barron: That's kind of you. Do you have a sense of what people ask in this session?

47
00:05:18.355 --> 00:05:27.494
Tomás Reyes: In Learning and Tutoring, usually two kinds of questions. Generalization: does this work beyond your course. And privacy: what do students know about being logged.

48
00:05:27.722 --> 00:05:30.821
Tomás Reyes: I saw your paper, so I'd expect both.

49
00:05:31.682 --> 00:05:36.713
David Barron: Yeah, that's, um, those were the two big things in the reviews too.

50
00:05:36.979 --> 00:05:44.457
David Barron: We added a limitations section and a cross-course analysis for the camera-ready, so I have a backup slide for each.

51
00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:51.608
Tomás Reyes: Good, backup slides are smart. Put them after your closing slide so you can jump to them.

52
00:05:52.806 --> 00:05:53.906
David Barron: Will do.

53
00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.448
Tomás Reyes: Anything else from your side?

54
00:05:57.709 --> 00:06:01.141
David Barron: Just, when should I be in the room?

55
00:06:06.092 --> 00:06:15.358
Tomás Reyes: Fifteen minutes before the session starts, so ten-fifteen. There's a speaker-ready table next to the lectern. Kai or someone from his team will be there.

56
00:06:15.853 --> 00:06:24.813
Kai (UIST AV): And if you want, you can come to the room during the coffee break on Tuesday and test your laptop on the real projector.

57
00:06:25.773 --> 00:06:28.287
David Barron: Oh, I'll do that, that's great.

58
00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:36.293
Tomás Reyes: Okay. I think we're done. Send me the bio, upload the backup by Monday, and see you Wednesday.

59
00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:42.087
David Barron: Thank you both. Bio today, backup by Monday, laptop test Tuesday at the break.

60
00:06:42.749 --> 00:06:44.175
Kai (UIST AV): See you there.

61
00:06:45.617 --> 00:06:46.954
Tomás Reyes: See you, David.

62
00:06:48.046 --> 00:06:50.028
David Barron: Okay, stopping the recording.
